phase P10
title Release
description
    **Class:** verifiable.

    **Kind:** ticket.

    **Goal:**

    - the package published, only as far as the user asks;
    - its published name decided then.

    **Starts when:** P9's completion audit passes.

    **Verified by:**

    - the packed-consumer check on the exact tarball;
    - `nub run verify`;
    - an independent review of the release change.

    **One iteration:** implement, check independently, repair.

    **Exit criteria:** acceptance passes at the final revision, and each requested ship stage is
    confirmed by the user.

    **False pass:** publishing a package whose installed form differs from what was tested.

    **Caught by:** the packed-consumer check.

    **Gates:** the packed-consumer check, which rejects a tarball packed with one entry point
    removed.

    **Budget:** the Epic's Budget section, row P10.

    **Failure limit:** 2.

    **Stops:** before each ship stage (publish, land, tag); the published name.

    **User's read:** none.

    **Draws from:** skill:playbook-ship; skill:review.
tasks
    T39
        title       Release as far as the user asks
        status      draft
        priority    medium
        labels      [verifiable, ticket]
        description
            Pack, run the packed-consumer check, and stop before each ship stage. Drafted in full
            when P10 starts.

            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** tested form differs from published → caught by the packed-consumer
              check.
            - **Gates:** the packed-consumer check.
            - **Budget:** one Task.
            - **Stops:** each ship stage; the published name.
            - **User's read:** none.
        acceptance
            The packed-consumer check passes on the exact tarball; each requested stage done.
